Calico is now deployed in eBPF mode.
For existing deployments running in iptables, ipvs or nftables mode,
a migration is necessary.
The migration is disruptive.

Run the following to perform the migration:

.. important::

   When performing a release migration (see :doc:`/user/guide/upgrade-release`),
   the Calico migration to the eBPF dataplane
   must be executed **before** running the :ref:`apply-all action <actions-references.apply-allsh>`.

.. important::

   During the migration, the default ``FelixConfiguration`` will be recreated
   which removes any manually added configuration.
   Custom configuration of the ``FelixConfiguration`` must be handled via
   :ref:`Calico's helm values <configuration-options.yk8s.kubernetes.network.calico.helm.values>`
   as the tigera-operator refuses to continue managing it
   if it detects manual changes.

.. code:: console

   $ MANAGED_K8S_RELEASE_THE_KRAKEN=true \
     ./managed-k8s/actions/apply-k8s-supplements.sh install-calico.yaml

_
